    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26-a4">

                <pb facs="0477" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv07/pg467"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–21</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="16" xml:id="d26-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-30">July 30, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">General Franchet d’Esperey to the
                        Minister of War</hi></p>
                <p>The decision of the Inter-Allied Supreme Council<anchor n="17" xml:id="d26-f2"/>
                    which you communicated to me on June 10 provided for the participation of
                    British and Italian troops in the occupation of Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>I decided to form for the occupation of Bulgarian Thrace a detachment composed of
                    two French battalions, of one Italian battalion of the 62nd Regiment of Infantry
                    stationed at Adrianople and designated by the Italian command, and of an English
                    detachment.</p>
                <p>The Italian General Headquarters advises me that the question of what effectives
                    are to be maintained in Turkey by Italy is being submitted to the Peace
                    Conference by the delegation of this Power, and <pb facs="0478" n="468"
                        xml:id="pg468"/> that there is no occasion in the meanwhile to withdraw the
                    battalion from Adrianople.</p>
                <p>On the other hand, the British command has not yet made known the effective force
                    of the detachment to be furnished by the British Army.</p>
                <p>Under these conditions, the French troops are going to be alone in bearing the
                    burden and the responsibility of the occupation of Bulgaria at the time of the
                    treaty of peace.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
